<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:s="https://wvusports.com/services/xml_schema/story" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title /><link>https://wvusports.com/rss/</link><description /><atom:link href="https://wvusports.com/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><language>en-us</language><ttl>60</ttl><item><title>Mountaineers Conclude Season With Loss at Utah</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/28/football-mountaineers-conclude-season-with-loss-at-utah</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/28/football-mountaineers-conclude-season-with-loss-at-utah</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="One of the few times West Virginia's defense was able to get to Utah quarterback Devon Dampier during tonight's loss to the second-ranked Utes in Salt Lake City, Utah." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/27/Dampier-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />Second-ranked Utah scored on all five of its first-half possessions in rolling to a 52-28 victory over West Virginia at Rice-Eccles Stadium in Salt Lake City, Utah.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/Dampier-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/Dampier-Main.jpg"><media:title>One of the few times West Virginia's defense was able to get to Utah quarterback Devon Dampier during tonight's loss to the second-ranked Utes in Salt Lake City, Utah.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/Dampier-Main.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Sat, 28 Nov 2026 00:35:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59772</s:story_id></item><item><title>WVU Falls Short Against Virginia in NCAA Second Round</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/27/womens-soccer-wvu-falls-short-against-virginia-in-ncaa-second-round</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/27/womens-soccer-wvu-falls-short-against-virginia-in-ncaa-second-round</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Jacey Rase passes the ball during a match at Virginia on Nov. 27." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/27/WVUvsVirginia-3.jpg" /><br /><br />CHARLOTTESVILLE, Va. – The No. 7-seed West Virginia University women's soccer team's 2026 NCAA Tournament run was cut short after a 1-0 loss to No. 2-seed Virginia in the Second Round at Kl&ouml;ckner Stadium in Charlottesville, Virginia, on Friday night.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/WVUvsVirginia-3.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/WVUvsVirginia-3.jpg"><media:title>Jacey Rase passes the ball during a match at Virginia on Nov. 27.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/WVUvsVirginia-3.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:59:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59771</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Defeat North Carolina in Charlotte</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/27/mens-basketball-mountaineers-defeat-north-carolina-in-charlotte</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/27/mens-basketball-mountaineers-defeat-north-carolina-in-charlotte</guid><category>Men's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Joson Sanon drives into the lane during the first half of Friday night's game against North Carolina in Charlotte, North Carolina." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/27/Sanon-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />If only West Virginia could play North Carolina all the time. The Mountaineers used some smothering defense and relentless work on the offensive glass to defeat the Tarheels 72-59 in the second annual Dick Vitale Invitational played at the Spectrum Center in Charlotte, North Carolina.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/Sanon-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/Sanon-Main.jpg"><media:title>Joson Sanon drives into the lane during the first half of Friday night's game against North Carolina in Charlotte, North Carolina.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/Sanon-Main.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 21:24:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>4</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59770</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Cap Regular Season in Four-Set Loss to Texas Tech</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/27/volleyball-mountaineers-cap-regular-season-in-four-set-loss-to-texas-tech</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/27/volleyball-mountaineers-cap-regular-season-in-four-set-loss-to-texas-tech</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WVU Volleyball celebrates Senior Day in the match against texas tech" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/27/DSC00282.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. - The West Virginia University volleyball team (13-15, 6-12 Big 12) fell to Texas Tech, 3-1, on Friday afternoon at Hope Coliseum in its regular-season finale. The Mountaineers dropped the match by set scores of 25-19, 22-25, 25-20 and 25-21.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/DSC00282.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/DSC00282.jpg"><media:title>WVU Volleyball celebrates Senior Day in the match against texas tech</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/DSC00282.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:25:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59769</s:story_id></item><item><title>FINAL: Mountaineers Lose to No. 2 Utah</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/27/football-game-day-mountaineers-face-no-2-utah-on-the-road</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/27/football-game-day-mountaineers-face-no-2-utah-on-the-road</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="A blue West Virginia football helmet on the field of Rice-Eccles Stadium in Salt Lake City, Utah, before West Virginia's game against Utah on Nov. 27, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/27/FB_WVUvsUtah_Nov27_2026_JS-29.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. — The West Virginia Mountaineers lost to No. 2 Utah to finish the 2026 regular season on Friday night.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/FB_WVUvsUtah_Nov27_2026_JS-29.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/FB_WVUvsUtah_Nov27_2026_JS-29.jpg"><media:title>A blue West Virginia football helmet on the field of Rice-Eccles Stadium in Salt Lake City, Utah, before West Virginia's game against Utah on Nov. 27, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/FB_WVUvsUtah_Nov27_2026_JS-29.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 12:00:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59767</s:story_id></item><item><title>Countdown to Kickoff: Mountaineers to Meet Second-Ranked Utah Tonight</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/27/football-countdown-to-kickoff-mountaineers-to-meet-second-ranked-utah-tonight</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/27/football-countdown-to-kickoff-mountaineers-to-meet-second-ranked-utah-tonight</guid><category>Football</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="A view of Rice-Eccles Stadium on the eve of West Virginia's game against second-ranked Utah on Friday, Nov. 27, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/27/Utah-Stadium.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The Great Talent Redistribution going on in college football right now as a result of Name, Image and Likeness (NIL) and direct revenue sharing requires a reexamination of things.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/Utah-Stadium.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/Utah-Stadium.jpg"><media:title>A view of Rice-Eccles Stadium on the eve of West Virginia's game against second-ranked Utah on Friday, Nov. 27, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/27/Utah-Stadium.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:24:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>2</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59768</s:story_id></item><item><title>West Virginia Drops First Game to No. 13 Notre Dame</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/womens-basketball-west-virginia-drops-first-game-to-no-13-notre-dame</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/womens-basketball-west-virginia-drops-first-game-to-no-13-notre-dame</guid><category>Women's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WBB Team during the Battle 4 Atlantis game against Notre Dame" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/26/Story_Photo.JPG" /><br /><br />PARADISE ISLAND, Bahamas – West Virginia battled back from a slow start and cut a 17-point halftime deficit to eight in the third quarter, but Notre Dame pulled away late for a 78-64 victory on Thursday at Atlantis Resort. The loss dropped WVU to 6-1 on the season.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/26/Story_Photo.JPG" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/26/Story_Photo.JPG"><media:title>WBB Team during the Battle 4 Atlantis game against Notre Dame</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/26/Story_Photo.JPG" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:12:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>9</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59766</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Host Texas Tech for Senior Day in Regular Season Finale</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/volleyball-mountaineers-host-texas-tech-for-senior-day-in-regular-season-finale</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/volleyball-mountaineers-host-texas-tech-for-senior-day-in-regular-season-finale</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Alexis Finnvold and Mirjam Kask high five after a point in the match against Baylor" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/26/ex1_75.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University volleyball team (13-14, 6-11 Big 12) closes out the 2026 regular season on Friday, Nov. 27, welcoming Texas Tech to Hope Coliseum for Senior Day. First serve is set for 3 p.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/26/ex1_75.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/26/ex1_75.jpg"><media:title>Alexis Finnvold and Mirjam Kask high five after a point in the match against Baylor</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/26/ex1_75.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 11:52:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59765</s:story_id></item><item><title>West Virginia-North Carolina to Meet in Charlotte on Friday Night</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/mens-basketball-west-virginia-north-carolina-to-meet-in-charlotte-on-friday-night</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/mens-basketball-west-virginia-north-carolina-to-meet-in-charlotte-on-friday-night</guid><category>Men's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="West Virginia guard Miles Sadler celebrates a basket during the Mountaineers' season-opening victory over Niagara at Hope Coliseum on Monday, Nov. 2, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/2/Sadler-Main.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – West Virginia meets North Carolina on Friday, Nov. 27, at the Spectrum Center in Charlotte, North Carolina, in the second annual Dick Vitale Invitational being put on by ESPN Events and the Charlotte Sports Foundation.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/2/Sadler-Main.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/2/Sadler-Main.jpg"><media:title>West Virginia guard Miles Sadler celebrates a basket during the Mountaineers' season-opening victory over Niagara at Hope Coliseum on Monday, Nov. 2, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/2/Sadler-Main.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:52:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>4</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59754</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Head to Charlottesville for Second Round of NCAA Tournament</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/womens-soccer-mountaineers-head-to-charlottesville-for-second-round-of-ncaa-tournament</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/26/womens-soccer-mountaineers-head-to-charlottesville-for-second-round-of-ncaa-tournament</guid><category>Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Layla Thompson dribbles a ball during a match." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/25/TG9_7916.jpg" /><br /><br />CHARLOTTESVILLE, Va. – The No. 7-seed West Virginia University women's soccer team continues its 25th NCAA Tournament appearance when it travels to No. 2-seed Virginia for the Second Round on Friday, Nov. 20. Kickoff at Kl&ouml;ckner Stadium in Charlottesville, Virginia, is slated for 6 p.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/25/TG9_7916.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/25/TG9_7916.jpg"><media:title>Layla Thompson dribbles a ball during a match.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/25/TG9_7916.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2026 10:14:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>13</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59764</s:story_id></item></channel></rss>